  "body_markdown": "(310)-481-0111\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4® Dental Implants\n\nHybrid Fixed Detachable Denture\n\nZirconia Fixed Bridge\n\nImplant Supported Dentures\n\nRobotic Surgery\n\nCost & Compare\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nFAQ\n\nAesthetic Dentistry\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers & Lumineers\n\nInvisalign\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nServices\n\nIV Sedation\n\nBone Grafting\n\nRidge Augmentation\n\nSinus Augmentation\n\nTooth Extractions\n\nGeneral Dentistry\n\nPeriodontics\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nMissing Teeth\n\nBone Loss\n\nFailing Dental Implants\n\nLoose Dentures\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nOur Facility\n\nPatient Stories\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\nWho We Are\n\nCommitment To Excellence\n\nMeet Dr. Tony Barriere\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nBlog\n\nContact Us\n\nPatient Portal\n\nNew Patients\n\nCurrent Patients\n\n\n## How Painful Is It to Get Dental Implants?\n\n\nFebruary 22, 2022\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nShare on facebook\n\nShare on linkedin\n\nShare on twitter\n\nShare on email\n\nDo you have a low tolerance for pain? Are you scared to correct your teeth because of the pain that may come from it? Have you heard horror stories about the pain that comes from dental implants?\n\nWell, everyone’s experience is different. You may or may not experience pain when it comes to dental implants. A dentist in Los Angeles, CA is more than happy to assist you with letting you know what the experience will be like when you get dental implants.\n\n\n## What Should You Expect While Getting Dental Implants?\n\n\nWhen you are having dental implantation surgery, it is usually done under local anesthesia, IV sedation, or general anesthesia which means you shouldn’t feel any pain during the dental implant surgery.\n\nWith recovery, there could be some pain and or discomfort and can last a few days, but it is often cured with using medication. If you have pain that lasts more than a few days and/or the pain gets worse, your team of dental professionals will be able to instruct you on the best plan to take. Post-surgical pain symptoms following dental implant surgery included:\n\nSurgery site bleeding\n\nFace and gum swelling\n\nMinor bruising\n\nPain in the jaw\n\nA proper after care routine will be given to you by the oral surgeon once the dental implant surgery is complete which will include but not be limited to:\n\nPain medications like over the counter or prescription\n\nTry to avoid hot or hard foods as much as possible\n\nReduce swelling with ice packs\n\nDepending on how you feel, rest the day of the procedure and maybe a few days after\n\nSurgical care site instructions\n\n\n## Interested In Learning More?\n\n\nAfter reading this article and noticing the pain is not as horror as it may sound, are you ready to jump-start your journey today and get your dental implants? Are you ready to smile like you have never smiled before?\n\nCall our doctor, Dr. Tony Barriere, in our office in Los Angeles, CA and schedule your consultation to start your journey to regain your confidence and smiling more!\n\nPrevPreviousWhat Do You Need to Get Dental Implants?\n\nNextDo I Have To Extract All My Teeth To Get Dental Implants?Next\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Are There Factors That Determine Which Type Of Dental Implant Procedure I Can Get Treated With?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a safe and effective way to replace missing or damaged teeth. They are\n\nRead More »\n\nAugust 20, 2023\n\n\n### Does Anything Happen To My Jawbone If I Don’t Immediately Replace My Missing Teeth With Dental Implants?\n\n\nDental implants in Los Angeles, FL, are a gold standard tooth replacement option that are surgically placed in a patient’s\n\nAugust 14, 2023\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nCall Now\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Yelp Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddress:\n\n12301 Wilshire Blvd Suite 205,\n\nL